  "rule_for_models": "Apply this PROMPT rule only to people aged 45 to 64 inclusive and, if age is missing, record that eligibility is unknown and do not report a PROMPT finding. Report possible duplication for two different ingredients in the same listed group or another known pharmacological class only when their treatment periods overlap or the difference between the two dispensing dates is 60 days or less. For opioids, apply the pain-use limits in Group A. Exclude a documented switch when the first medicine stopped before the second started. Keep the 60-day window when combined use is uncertain. Exclude short-acting plus long-acting beta-2 agonists for asthma or COPD and pairs used together for a documented guideline-supported additive effect.",
  "cannot_be_seen": "Why each medicine was prescribed, whether a guideline supports using the pair together, medicines supplied by a hospital or another pharmacy, and medicines bought without a prescription.",
  "ask_the_gp": "A review of whether both medicines from the same class are needed, or whether one can stop.",
  "urgency": "routine",
  "draft": false,
  "signed_by_clinical_reviewer": { "name": "Marwan Morsy (PHA0002761764)", "date": "2026-11-21" }
